WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.666
Hi! Today we're going to multiply a fraction by a fraction.

2
00:00:06.816 --> 00:00:16.074
Three quarters of the garden is a flower bed. Two thirds of the flower bed has roses. What fraction of the whole garden has roses?

3
00:00:16.224 --> 00:00:23.682
Draw a rectangle for the garden. Split it into 4 columns and shade 3. That is three quarters.

4
00:00:23.832 --> 00:00:30.930
Now split it into 3 rows, and shade 2 rows inside the flower bed. That is two thirds of the bed.

5
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:40.242
The whole garden now has 12 small squares, and the roses cover 6 of them. That is 6 twelfths, which is one half.

6
00:00:40.392 --> 00:00:51.858
The rule is: top times top, bottom times bottom. 2 times 3 is 6, 3 times 4 is 12. That gives 6 twelfths, which simplifies to one half.

7
00:00:52.008 --> 00:00:59.778
We can also simplify first. There is a 3 on the top and a 3 on the bottom, so we cancel them to make it easier.

8
00:00:59.928 --> 00:01:10.074
Improper fractions work the same way. 3 halves times 4 fifths is 12 tenths, which is 6 fifths, or 1 and 1 fifth.

9
00:01:10.224 --> 00:01:18.474
One more: four fifths of a plot grows vegetables, and half of that is tomatoes. What fraction of the plot is tomatoes?

10
00:01:18.624 --> 00:01:22.290
Half of it means one half times four fifths.

11
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:30.402
1 times 4 is 4, and 2 times 5 is 10. 4 tenths simplifies to 2 fifths.

12
00:01:30.552 --> 00:01:37.722
Watch out! Some pupils add the tops and add the bottoms, and get 5 sevenths. That is wrong!

13
00:01:37.872 --> 00:01:44.202
For multiplying, it's top times top and bottom times bottom. The answer is one half.

14
00:01:44.352 --> 00:01:51.234
Check: when you multiply by a fraction less than 1, the answer gets smaller.

15
00:01:51.384 --> 00:02:00.210
Your turn! What is 5 sixths times 3 tenths? Pause and think.

16
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:11.010
5 times 3 is 15, and 6 times 10 is 60. 15 sixtieths simplifies to one quarter. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:19.914
Another one! What is 3 quarters times 2 ninths? Pause and think.

18
00:02:20.064 --> 00:02:30.666
3 times 2 is 6, and 4 times 9 is 36. 6 thirty-sixths simplifies to 1 sixth. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:39.450
Last one! What is 2 fifths times 5 eighths? Pause and think.

20
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:49.554
Top times top is 10, and bottom times bottom is 40. 10 fortieths simplifies to 1 quarter. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:49.704 --> 00:02:59.994
Remember: to multiply fractions, multiply the tops and multiply the bottoms. Simplify first if you can, and give the answer in its simplest form.

22
00:03:00.144 --> 00:03:04.338
Now go and practise in your garden!

